अदृश्य ब्रह्मांड का नक्शा (Mapping the Invisible Universe), a film by ExplainEveryday.
Every picture is drawn in code (SVG); no photos, no ESA images, no video model.

Film style grammar: Scale Zoom Explainer, from the Lemo-Opuscar library (render, mix and mux tools used as tools; see that library's LICENSE for its own terms).

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1, self-hosted in fonts/):
- Jost, by Owen Earl (Google Fonts, ofl/jost)
- Noto Sans Devanagari, by Google (Google Fonts, ofl/notosansdevanagari)

Narration voice: Microsoft Edge neural text-to-speech, voice hi-IN-SwaraNeural, through the edge-tts package (online service). The voice is a synthetic voice.
Speech check only: faster-whisper (Whisper "small" model), not part of the film.

Music: an original score played from free sample libraries (sampler.py):
Samples (CC0): FreePats project (freepats.zenvoid.org), VS Chamber Orchestra: Community Edition (Versilian Studios), Versilian Community Sample Library (Versilian Studios)
No background music. Sound effects are synthesised procedurally.

Facts: see FACTS.md. The film names ESA's Euclid mission and India's GMRT (NCRA-TIFR) only in words; no logos or imagery from either are used.
The user is responsible for the materials they use in their own films.
